<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        ellekit filter plist for VcamFullMay.

        Lessons learned via live testing on Dopamine 2 / ellekit 1.1.3:

        1. `Filter > Bundles` matches FRAMEWORK bundle IDs (e.g. com.apple.UIKit),
           NOT the app's own CFBundleIdentifier — listing app IDs there
           matched nothing.
        2. `Filter > Executables` did not match running apps either — likely
           not supported by ellekit at all.
        3. The reliable pattern is: broad-inject via UIKit framework filter,
           then *inside %ctor* check `[NSBundle mainBundle].bundleIdentifier`
           against an allowlist. Tweaks like Choicy follow this pattern.

        We do both:
          - This filter targets `com.apple.UIKit` so ellekit injects us into
            every UIKit-loading process.
          - Tweak.xm's %ctor calls `vcam_unsafe_host()` (skip shells/system
            tools) and `vcam_target_app()` (skip non-target apps) before
            installing any hooks. Non-target apps see a no-op dylib.
    -->
    <key>Filter</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Bundles</key>
        <array>
            <string>com.apple.UIKit</string>
        </array>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
